From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ppenguin <hieronymusv@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:14:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(samba): share accounts and per-share restriction

Every share here is authenticated (guest access is off), but nothing
could grant access: there was no way to create a Samba account, and a
share was open to any account Samba happened to know.

Share accounts are system accounts that exist only to mount shares:
separate from the CasaOS login, no home directory, a nologin shell, and
marked in GECOS so the API never re-keys or removes any other account
of the machine (root included). Passwords go to smbpasswd's standard
input, never into the process table. A share can be restricted to one
account; it is rendered as `valid users` + `force user` together (one
without the other leaves the share open to every account, or hands the
files to whoever connected). A share without an account renders exactly
as before, and existing rows read back with an empty account.

The share's top directory goes to its account (account:account, 0770)
when it is restricted, and back to root (0755) when the restriction is
lifted or the share removed: with force user, a root-owned directory
would authenticate and then refuse every write. It changes through the
pinned management roots (fchown/fchmod on the opened directory), inside
the same transaction, and is restored if publishing fails. Nothing
below the top directory is touched.

API: GET/POST /v1/samba/users, PUT /v1/samba/users/:username/password,
DELETE /v1/samba/users/:username (refused while a share names the
account), PUT /v1/samba/shares/:id {"username"}, and "username" on
share creation. Changing a share's account publishes the fragment in
the same transaction as the row, with the existing rollback.

nologin is looked up in its usual locations (incl. NixOS's) before
PATH, so the accounts' shell does not point into a package store.

Ported from the ReCasaOS distribution (ReCasaOS/CasaOS 5a7c55c,
20df217: "let a share be restricted to a dedicated account"), adapted to
this fork's authenticated-only shares and transactional publication.
Stacked on "external Samba main config (include-only mode)".

Co-Authored-By: Gary <contact@ixelia.fr>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
